    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27208" root="طه" body-key="T">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَهْطَهَ</span></b>  <i>He laughed immoderately:</i> (L
voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَدْكَدَ</span>:) or you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَهْطَهَ فِى ضَحِكِهِ</span>,
meaning <i>he laughed slightly;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْطَحَ</span>. (O
and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طح</span>.)

